<div{{ attributes }}>
    <ul>
        {#
            `computed` is a proxy that wraps your component and caches the return of 
            methods. If they are called additional times, the cached value is used.

            Note: computed methods only work for component methods with no required arguments.

            Note: do not use the ExposeInTemplate attribute on a computed method, otherwise 
                the method will be called twice instead of only once.

            Note: to help LiveComponents understand which element is which between re-renders 
                 (i.e. if something re-orders or removes some of those elements), you can add 
                 a key attribute to each element.

            Note: When live components re-renders, if the props passed into that component haven't 
                 changed, it doesn't see any reason to re-render it

                 In order the force re-rendering of a component:
                   1. Make the key dynamic so it will be different
                   2. Reset the state of the component

            The system doesn't handle every edge case in re-rendering, so here are some things to 
            keep in mind:

            1. If JavaScript changes an attribute on a child element, that change is preserved.

            2. If JavaScript adds a new element, that element is preserved.

            3. If JavaScript removes an element that was originally rendered by the component, that 
               change will be lost: the element will be re-added during the next re-render.

            4. If JavaScript changes the text of an element, that change is lost: it will be restored 
               to the text from the server during the next re-render.

            5. If an element is moved from one location in the component to another, that change is lost: 
               the element will be re-added in its original location during the next re-render.
        #}
        {% for product in computed.products %}
            <li key="{{ product.id }}>{{ product.name | capitalize }}: {{ product.price }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>
</div>
